{
  "name": "NamedValuesBelongToTheType",
  "comment": "Named values belong to their type (ruling 3). separator becomes a text — it goes under\ntext, with its named values (\"line\", \"comma\", \"tab\", \"space\", \"semicolon\") held as its\nown list. The proof stage 2 names: `%line% is text` is true (red today — separator is\nits own top-level type today, deriving from item, not text).",
